## 7. DAY-TO-DAY RESPONSIBILITIES, 2035–2045

**Pre-crew phase (2035–2038).** Primary role is Autonomous City Operator. Monitor robotic construction progress via digital twin; authorize zone expansions; manage sequencing of power, ISRU, and road completion. Every decision is made through the twin because there is no other access to the surface. The city is being built, and no human has ever stood in it.

**First crew phase (2038–2040).** Primary role shifts to Habitat Integration Director. Integrate human occupancy zones into already-operating robotic infrastructure. Design EVA corridors that do not conflict with autonomous vehicle routes. The city was built for robots and must now be adapted, in real time, for people — without stopping the robots.

**Growth phase (2040–2045).** Primary role becomes City Governor. Manage expansion from outpost to settlement. Zone new districts for science, manufacturing, and residence. Develop interoperability standards for incoming international modules and assets. The city is now a political object as well as a physical one.

**Crisis response (ongoing).** When power, communications, or life support triggers an anomaly, the City Architect's cascade failure model determines which zones to isolate, which to protect at all costs, and in what order to restore function. This is not an emergency role — it is the permanent background function of the profession, running in parallel with all other responsibilities.

